# What the Comfy Registry package leaves out (gitwildmatch, read by comfy-cli's `comfy node publish`).
# The package keeps what ComfyUI loads - __init__.py, pyproject.toml, plenio/, web/, subgraphs/,
# example_workflows/, resources/, locales/ - plus the licence files, README, CHANGELOG and the user guide.
# Patterns start with "/" so they only match at the repository root (an unanchored `assets/`
# also dropped plenio/core/assets and broke the import - found by installing the packed zip).
# The Studio add-on - the functions that start a program (ComfyUI from the player, a llama-server, the file
# manager) - is part of a git clone and of the release zip only; the Registry package starts nothing but its own
# Python with Plenio's own modules (plenio/core/features.py, tools/package_gate.py).
/plenio/addons/
# The two start scripts of the player run on their own (they pick the Python beside ComfyUI): part of the full
# download too. The package's player is opened from ComfyUI, or with `python plenio_player.py`.
/Plenio Player.bat
/plenio_player.sh
/.github/
/CLAUDE.md
/.gitattributes
/tests/
/tools/
/frontend/
/assets/
/docs/*
!/docs/user/
